    {
      "id": "shown-out",
      "type": "story",
      "position": {
        "x": 1260,
        "y": 840
      },
      "data": {
        "kind": "exit",
        "title": "Shown the door",
        "description": "Last resort. The investigator has thrown the morning away: made a scene he can't overlook (steel drawn or a blow struck in his dressing room, at Master Sallow or anyone; the King threatened; the case shouted from the windows to the delegations or the crowd), or walked out on the King before telling him what they found. The Marshal has them shown down the back stairs, and the King goes down to the procession with nothing settled; whatever they found waits on Kell's notebook. This is the end of the story.",
        "closing": "Close the story, short and quiet: the back stairs, the door shut behind them, the bells beginning, and the procession going out without them. Then, in a few sentences, what became of the people the player's choices touched, going only by what happened, each in a line. Don't soften it, and don't narrate beyond it. Then: The End.",
        "result": "bad",
        "exitKind": "other",
        "effects": [
          {
            "op": "quest",
            "quest": "purveyors-man",
            "do": "fail",
            "text": "Shown out of the King's dressing room before the bells, with nothing settled: Master Sallow's business waits until after the Assembly, if anyone looks into it at all."
